    "description": "Some Parisian addresses are truly exceptional, and certain views cannot be described they must be experienced.\n\nJust a few metres from the Eiffel Tower, this 204 m² air-conditioned reception flat is situated on the fifth floor (with lift access) of a luxury Haussmann-style building dating from 1900. It offers a quintessentially Parisian experience, blending timeless elegance with the Rive Gauche lifestyle.\n\nThe moment you step inside, the light takes centre stage.\nThe proportions are majestic: 3.20-metre-high ceilings, herringbone parquet flooring, mouldings, fireplaces and natural light flooding through.\n\nThe eye is immediately drawn to the Eiffel Tower, visible from every angle, whether from the reception rooms or the master suite.\n\nThe double living room and dining room, facing south-west, open onto an elegant 11.5 m² balcony for intimate dinners suspended above the greenery, with spectacular views of the Eiffel Tower, the Seine and the Trocadéro.\n\nThe kitchen, designed to evoke a country house in the heart of the capital, subtly blends French style, fine materials and shades of celadon green.\n\nThe sleeping area comprises:\na stunning master suite with a view of the Eiffel Tower and an en-suite shower room,\na second suite with an en-suite shower room,\na third bedroom with a separate bathroom that can be joined to the second suite,\nas well as a dressing room or a fourth bedroom.\na utility room\n\nConcierge, lift, majestic communal areas, secure building, 2 cellars.\n\nJust a stone’s throw from the Champ-de-Mars, the banks of the Seine, the upmarket shops of Rue Saint-Dominique and Paris’s finest international schools.\n\nA rare, light-filled and quintessentially Parisian property in one of the capital’s most iconic locations.",
