    "description": "Set in unspoilt surroundings where water, nature and heritage come together, this remarkable château stands as one of the finest examples of the evolution of French architecture between the late Middle Ages and the dawn of French Classicism.\n\nOverlooking the banks of a river, the property has its origins in an ancient fortress, of which an imposing 15th-century keep still stands. In the early 17th century, a prominent aristocratic family undertook an ambitious transformation of the site, giving it its present appearance: a noble residence with balanced proportions where elegance and architectural rigour blend harmoniously.\n\nFrom the moment you enter, the spacious rooms impress with their precision and authenticity. The layout is organised around a spectacular central staircase leading to vast reception areas and apartments steeped in history. As you move through the rooms, exposed beamed ceilings, original floors, period fireplaces, refined wood panelling and decorative features, patiently preserved or enhanced over the centuries—are revealed, lending the whole property a rare and timeless atmosphere.\n\nDesigned to accommodate life in a château in all its splendour, the residence boasts exceptional proportions. It features 15 bedrooms and 12 bathrooms, whilst the main reception rooms and the dining room each span nearly 100 m², offering spectacular spaces dedicated to both entertaining and family life.\nThe estate surrounding the château creates a setting of great poetic beauty. Genuine moats, a feature that has become particularly rare in large historic estates, surround the residence and serve as a reminder of its defensive past. A fully restored keep watches over the grounds, whilst an elegant orangery offers a wealth of possibilities for hosting receptions, private events or cultural gatherings. The rows of trees, the classically inspired gardens, the orchard, the kitchen garden and the wooded areas create a structured landscape where every view seems to have been designed to enhance the house.\n\nFew properties have survived the centuries with such integrity. A true testament to the French art of living, this château now offers far more than just an exceptional residence: a unique experience, shaped by four centuries of history, architecture and heritage. 20 minutes from Parthenay, 25 minutes from Bressuire and Thouars, and 1 hour from Poitiers.",
