    "description": "This villa is a striking contemporary residence set within the prestigious, pine-shaded enclave of Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat, one of the most exclusive peninsulas on the French Riviera. Completed in 2022 on a design by architect Pascal Goujon, the villa presents a minimalist, cubic architecture wrapped in a signature semi-transparent timber screen facade, offering privacy without sacrificing light. Inside, 327 m² of meticulously composed living space unfolds across four levels plus a rooftop, each room considered for its symmetry, flow and relationship to the sea. \n\nThe garden level is the heart of the home: an open kitchen and spacious living and dining salon sit at pool level and open directly onto a generous terrace, dissolving the line between indoors and out. \n\nTwo ensuite bedrooms, each with its own dressing room and private terrace, occupy the floor above, while the uppermost level is reserved for a sea-view Primary Bedroom suite with dressing room and bathroom, alongside a second bedroom flexible enough to serve as a private lounge. \n\nBelow, an independent gym with its own shower and WC, a wine cellar and discreet technical spaces complete the accommodation. Crowning the villa, a rooftop terrace with outdoor lounge and barbecue area delivers one of the peninsula's most privileged panoramic sea views. The interior decoration is warm, luminous and Southern in spirit, with a natural palette that plays beautifully against the Mediterranean light. \n\nThis villa also holds a rare distinction for a Riviera property of this caliber: an A-rated energy performance certificate, with estimated annual running costs of under €1,300 — genuine efficiency to match its architectural pedigree. \n\nA rare pairing of design, comfort and privacy on Cap Ferrat.",
