    "tokenContractAddress": "0x7a7a7a7a7a7a7a7a7a7a7a7a7a7a7a7a83cae0b1",
    "description": "Iconic 16th- 18th Century Perche Castle That Hosted Sun King’s Son\nFormer residence of the Viscount of Perche – Listed Historic Monument, 42-hectare estate set atop a commanding hilltop, between Normandy and Loire Valley, famous touristic landmark. \n\n2h from Paris, Overlooking the surrounding countryside from the summit of a hill, Château des Feugerets occupies a strategic and historically significant position, this remarkable property reflects an ancient seigneurial heritage, enhanced by noble architectural developments from the 16th and 17th centuries and refined interiors dating from the 18th and 19th centuries.\n\nLocated within a designated remarkable natural site, in the heart of a regional natural park, the estate benefits from an exceptional landscape setting and a dominant position offering far-reaching views over the Norman countryside.\n\nThe property is officially listed as a Historic Monument, recognizing its architectural and historical significance.\n\nSurrounded by dry moats, the château stands out for its elegant silhouette, highlighted by a Versailles-style balustraded terrace and a majestic horseshoe staircase in the Louis XIII style, emblematic features of grand French residences.\n\n⸻\n\nThe Château – Architectural elegance and reception volumes\n\nOffering approximately 1,150 sq m (12,380 sq ft) of living space, the château provides prestigious reception areas ideally suited for refined private living or high-end hospitality and events.\n\nReception rooms in enfilade\n\n* Five reception salons\n* Two dining rooms\n* Billiard room\n\nLayout\n\n* Three staircases\n* 11 bedrooms (plus the 4 attic rooms to renovate)\n* 5 bathrooms and 6wc\n* 18th century living, dining room and Library \n* 19th century Chapel \n\n⸻\n\nRemarkable architectural and decorative features\n\nThe interiors display a remarkable state of preservation, showcasing the elegance of the 18th and 19th centuries.\n\nNotable features include:\n\n* Superb period wood paneling\n* Marble fireplaces\n* Original hardwood parquet flooring\n* Decorative moldings and ceilings\n* Alcoves\n* Numerous preserved historic architectural details\n\nThe property reflects the harmonious evolution of a historic residence that has retained its authenticity and character.\n\n⸻\n\nOutbuildings – A comprehensive and versatile estate complex\n\nThe estate is distinguished by the quality and diversity of its outbuildings, forming a rare and highly functional ensemble suitable for residential, hospitality, or event-related use.\n\n⸻\n\nTwo independent houses\n\nCaretaker’s house\n\n* Independent four-room house\n\nAssociated outbuildings\n\n* Kennel\n* Garage\n* Fruit storehouse\n* Barn\n* Storage building\n* Woodshed\n* Small livestock shelter\n\n⸻\n\nHistoric lower courtyard (16th century)\n\nLocated below the château, the lower courtyard forms a remarkable architectural ensemble composed of two historic wings and two pavilions, arranged around a structured courtyard.\n\nRight wing – Stables and service buildings\n\n* 19th-century stables\n* Five horse boxes and stalls\n* Washhouse\n* Tack room (saddlery)\n* Former hunting room\n* Storage buildings\n* Barn\n* Garage\n\nLeft wing – Renovated event facility\n\nThe left wing of the lower courtyard has been renovated and now offers flexible professional use, particularly suited to hosting events or public gatherings.\n\nIt includes:\n\n* Large reception hall of approximately 100 sq m (1,076 sq ft), classified as an ERP (public-access building)\n* Sanitary facilities compliant with public use\n* Traditional bread oven\n* Kitchen\n* Storage room\n* Former bedroom\n\nBasement level\n\n* Cellars located beneath the building, providing additional storage or operational space\n\nThis facility represents a major asset for hospitality, cultural, or event-based activities, with infrastructure already adapted to public reception standards.\n\n⸻\n\nParkland and land – Exceptional 42-hectare estate\n\nThe estate extends over approximately 42 hectares (about 104 acres) in one continuous holding, within a protected and highly desirable natural environment.\n\nLand composition\n\n* 2.5-hectare landscaped English-style park enclosed by stone walls \n* 20 hectares of woodland (free)\n* 20 hectares of enclosed pastureland (free)\n* Ornamental gardens and parterres\n* Hunting rights\n\nLandscape features\n\n* Greenhouse and vegetable garden\n* Orangery\n* Sheepfold\n* Cedar tree officially designated as a “Remarkable Tree of France”\n* Duck pond\n* Scenic views from an elevated and dominant position\n\n⸻\n\nComfort and technical features\n\nThe property benefits from technical improvements enhancing comfort and operational efficiency while respecting the historic character of the estate.\n\nComfort and equipment\n\n* Heating system with five heat pumps\n* Attic insulation completed\n* Partial double glazing\n* High-speed fiber-optic internet connection\n* Recently installed heated swimming pool with terrace\n* Double glass windows on half the castle and all in outbuildings \n* New soils on the ground floor \n* Heated Swimming pool with terrasse \n\nThese features ensure year-round comfort, suitable for primary residence, secondary residence, or hospitality operations.\nThe castle runs a small commercial activity : bed and breakfast, weddings venue, temporary exhibition, art festival and guided tours (it is one the main touristic landmark of the Perche area) and is well maintened.\n\n⸻\n\nPositioning – A major historic estate\n\nFormer seigneurial residence of the Viscount of Perche, established in a commanding hilltop position, Château des Feugerets represents a significant heritage property combining:\n\n* Prestigious medieval origins\n* Official Historic Monument listing\n* 42-hectare estate in a single holding\n* Renaissance and Grand Siècle architecture\n* Existing event infrastructure (ERP classification)\n* Comprehensive outbuildings\n* Dominant hilltop setting\n* Modern technical upgrades\n\n——\nCommercial activity running : \nBed and breakfast, weddings venue, art exhibition and guided tours with current incomes. \n\n\nA rare opportunity on the international market for historic French estates, suited to discerning buyers seeking authenticity, privacy, and long-term patrimonial value.",
