    "description": "PARIS 7TH – AVENUE RAPP\n\nIn the heart of the Gros-Caillou neighborhood, just steps from the Champ-de-Mars, Rue Saint-Dominique, and Rue Cler, this magnificent 189.91-square-meter apartment—approximately 2,044 square feet under the Carrez Law—is located on the fourth floor of an elegant and secure period building with an elevator and resident caretaker.\n\nCompletely redesigned by an architect, the apartment offers a highly refined interpretation of Parisian elegance. The renovation pairs the property’s original character—chevron-pattern hardwood floors, decorative moldings, period fireplaces, and stained-glass windows—with a contemporary aesthetic defined by curved lines, natural tones, and custom millwork.\n\nA spacious entry gallery leads to generous entertaining spaces with a southwesterly exposure. The living and dining rooms create a beautifully harmonious reception area, enhanced by oversized windows, period fireplaces, and custom built-ins. From the avenue-facing rooms, the Eiffel Tower rises above the rooftops of Paris.\n\nOpening directly onto the gallery, the fully equipped eat-in kitchen blends seamlessly with the apartment’s architecture. Its light wood cabinetry, concealed storage, and sculptural island create a space that is both sophisticated and highly functional.\n\nThe private quarters comprise three bedroom suites, each with its own en suite bathroom or shower room, as well as extensive custom storage.\n\nFacing the avenue and enjoying a southwesterly exposure, the first suite is filled with natural light and offers a privileged view of the Eiffel Tower. It features built-in closets and a private shower room.\n\nQuietly positioned overlooking the courtyard, the second suite has been designed as an intimate and fully self-contained space. It also features custom storage and an elegant shower room finished in soft, natural tones.\n\nThe primary suite, measuring more than 30 square meters, features an expansive custom dressing room and a remarkable open-concept bathroom designed as a private wellness retreat, complete with a freestanding soaking tub and a beautifully appointed vanity area.\n\nA laundry room, separate powder room, extensive storage, and a large cellar complete the property.\n\nEvery detail has been carefully considered to provide effortless, discreet comfort, including smart-home technology, an integrated sound system, architectural lighting, double-pane windows, and radiant floor heating in the bathrooms.\n\nThe apartment is offered fully furnished. Its sculptural furnishings and custom-designed features complement and extend the architectural vision throughout.\n\nA separate service room on the eighth floor is also included in the sale. Measuring 11.02 square meters under the Carrez Law—approximately 119 square feet—and 14.32 square meters, or approximately 154 square feet, of total floor area, it is equipped with a kitchenette, shower, and WC.\n\nA coveted address, an exceptional renovation, and one of Paris’s most iconic views come together in this sophisticated family and entertaining residence, offered fully furnished and move-in ready.",
